I always try to kill the riders from far away. Usually with a gun. In my
last ascension, Death and Pestilence actually were standing in a row.
"You shoot six +5 bullets: The first bullet hits Death! The second
bullet hits Death! The ...   The fifth bullet hits Death! You kill
Death! The sixth bullet hits Pestilence!" Very satisfying. Then I shot
another five bullets in the same turn (being very fast) and disposed of
Pestilence, for the time being. Neither of the riders ever managed to
take a single hit point from me, but to have enough room to simply shoot
them, my pet solar helped a lot, because he took out most of the other
adversaries (and Famine, twice).

> Undead slayer is not an easy role to play, but the Stake is a good weapon and the drain/sickness resistance are nice. 

Until you meet Demogorgon. Then undead slayers and necromancers are
about the best roles you can have. And Pestilence becomes much less
intimidating. Also you do not have to worry about rot worms in the Wyrm
Caves. (I was once so immersed in fighting the dragons in the Caves that
